mmates that got  into this career for money ended up  being killed and the only ones left  standing with those like him who had  strong convictions when it comes to  denji he obviously doesn't have any of  that and so although Aki is disgusted by  him he's also kind of trying to help him  in his own way because you know if denji  quits then at least he won't be murdered  by a devil following that he lights  another cigarette as he walks away but  before he can leave denji attacks his  balls with full force from behind one  thing we need to understand about denji  is that he has absolutely no code of  honor or anything like that so he has no  problem aiming for hack he's not the  entire fight as he continues to kick he  makes it clear that although his reasons  for being a devil Hunter might be  shallow it's still this job that allows  him to live his dream life so far on his  first day he's been able to have a  proper breakfast flirt with a girl and  get some brand new clothes which already  makes this a million times better than  working for the Yakuza because of that  he's not willing to give up his new life  so easily and NG keeps kicking akkie in  the balls until he gradually passes out  one interesting thing that was heavily  implied from their exchange is that Aki  also has a crush on mackuma as well so  his motivation to beat dengiarp is  partly fueled by jealousy especially  after she flirted with Dengue right in  front of him later on in the episode he  also gets loudly offended when he hears  that she gave denji a hug so yeah the  jealousy thing is definitely an element  in what's going on here some time later  back at HQ even though these two clearly  don't get along makima carries on with  her plan of putting denji into Aki's  unit within Public Safety there are  multiple units that each serve different  purposes and the team denji is joining  his special division 4 which is an exp  environmental Squad filled with the  weirdest people they have this place is  the best fit for Dengue mainly due to  his unusual talents and his weird  personality and so makima was always  going to put him there regardless of  whether Aki likes him or not in this  meeting makama then goes on to  explicitly confirm what we already knew  which is that if denji ever quits Public  Safety or disobeys his orders then he'll  be killed by them as if he was a devil  what this means is that for the rest of  his life he'll be working for them and  is presumably never allowed to retire  and you can tell from Aki's expression  that even he was surprised by this after  the meeting we then get confirmation  that these two will be living together  from this point forward and like makima  said if denji tries to run then Aki has  permission to kill him in that sense  chainsaw man is now totally the prisoner  of the Japanese government and as he  walks down the street he begins to  question machama's morality on the one  hand she has been kind to him and  treated him with more respect than the  Yakuza did but on the other side she's  also proven that she's willing to  sacrifice him if he doesn't do what she  says this confusion causes him to ask  Aki whether he thinks she's a bad person  but but considering that Aki also has a  crush on her I don't see a scenario  where he doesn't say that she's a good  person because denji has a simple mind  he takes this statement at face value  and chooses to think about the time she  was nice to him while disregarding all  the blatant threats she made to his life  now the next morning at Aki's house he  begins to fully live out his dreams but  in the process he triggers his new  roommate in a handful of different ways  for a start denji raised the kitchen to  create his ultimate toast which is  basically toast top with marmalade honey  butter cinnamon and three different  types of jam remember just a couple days  earlier he thought that putting jam on  his bread is something he'd never be  able to afford to do so to have all  these toppings is like a once in a  lifetime experience by itself that  probably doesn't get on Aki's nerves but  what annoys him is that denji kind of  just leaves the leftover mess all over  the living room table and he's super  loud when using the bath not to mention  that he also fell asleep while using the  toilet and then didn't replace the  missing toilet paper considering that  this is the first day of living together  you can tell that Aki doesn't feel  comfortable with the situation going on  hence why later in the episode he tries  to set denji up before we get to that  though the two of them are called out by  the police to deal with the fiend in my  last episode review I explained what a  fiend is but in case you haven't seen  that a fiend is a type of devil that  possesses the dead corpse of a human in  nearly all cases ifeen will have the  devil's personality and distinct  features on their head that lets  everyone know what they are this is  completely different to denji who still  retains his own personality and doesn't  have any weird features on his face  enabling him to mostly appear like a  normal human as he and Aki then arrive  at the house where the fiend is hiding  we see that an unknown devil has  possessed the body of a random  middle-aged man in the background  there's a cage for the bird that it's  currently eating and on the floor there  are tons of explicit magazines that  denji instantly notices not wanting to  get them dirty with blood he decides to  cleanly chop off this devil's head with  an ax rather than using his messy  chainsaws but when Aki questions that  decision Genji decides not to tell him  the truth maybe he thinks that Aki would  try to take the magazines for himself or  something but whatever the reason denji  pretends like he only killed the devil  this way to give it a painless death  this triggers Aki again because like we  established she hates Devils more than  anything and so for him to see a devil  Hunter sympathizing with Devils it makes  him even more suspicious of dengue than  he already was in reality though  chainsaw man didn't carry him the  slightest about the devil he killed but  I guess this cover story was needed to  hide his true horny motivations  following this denji has a moment of  self-reflection where he remembers his  contract with Vegeta and I guess the  issue here if you can call it that is  that he's already fulfilled his contract  within just a couple days what Vegeta  wanted was for denji to show him his  dreams which is something he's already  doing by you know eating good food  getting to watch himself getting to hang  around makima and just doing normal  things outside of work despite achieving  this perfect life he still feels like  there might be something missing which  plays into what he said in episode 1  when he realized that people will always  dream about having a better life no  matter how good their current life might  be this train of thought leads him to  wonder what his next true goal might be  and after thinking about makima he comes  to the conclusion that his real serious  goal in life is to touch her Booth  honestly I think I might have had a  similar dream to this at one point so  I'm not gonna act like it's that strange  especially considering that a hug is the  most he's ever gotten because of dendy's  previous financial situation he'd  completely given up on the idea of a  girl allowing him to touch her melons  but now that he has a good job the odds  are in his favor if he takes it  seriously this is where power comes in  as later in the episode she becomes his  new buddy at work thanks to ackee's  personal recommendation Genji and power  are paired up to patrol the neighborhood  for devils and what makes her special is  that she's not actually a Human Instead  power is a highly intelligent fiend  who's possessed the dead body of a  teenage girl but after zooming in on her  chest none of that matters to denji as  he views this as his best chance to  fulfill his brand new Dream On a related  No it should be said that no ordinary  theme would choose to become a devil  Hunter but due to Maxima's threats  Powers kind of been forced into this  lifestyle in that sense her and engine  in the same situation and that they're  both experiments who mcamer is testing  to see if they can do the job but if  they don't live up to her expectations  then yeah she's probably gonna kill them  in any case dengy and his new buddy then  start patrolling the rooftops for devils  and straight away it becomes clear just  how unpredictable power is although it's  true that she's smarter than the average  fiend she's still primarily motivated by  her basic double instincts which are to  kill things and to eat things that's why  she erratically runs around looking for  something to kill whether it be a devil  or a human I'm guessing and from this  Behavior denji realizes pretty early on  that she's a bit crazy but he's willing  to tolerate that craziness if it means  he gets to touch the melons as they  continue to walk they then come across  this cat just chilling on the roof and  although denji walked straight past it  power intensely stares at it and even if  she keeps walking her head is still  facing backwards this Fascination is  foreshadowing that cats are the only  animal she gets along with and this will  likely be explored further in the  episode next week for now though the two  of them keep searching the area for  Devils but they eventually take a break  after they can't find his single one  given that tracking down and capturing  Devils is pretty much their whole job  both their lives are at risk if they  can't get the results that Malcolm is  looking for in this scene power reveals  that the devils are likely avoiding them  because of her because back in the day  she used to be a powerful Devil with the  manga confirming that she was the blood  devil as you'd expect the blood devil  represents Humanity's fear of blood and  there are a decent amount of people out  there who do have this particular fear  it's not uncommon for people to faint  when they see blood or avoid situations  that would cause blood to be exposed and  all of that fear contributes to the  blood Devil's strength according to her  this strength is enough to scare the  weaker Devils away and while she could  be lying there is a reason why I think  she's at least partly telling the truth  remember denji and power will only  paired together because Aki suggested it  and if Powell's presence causes Devils  to run away then it means denji is less  likely to get results in that way Aki  has potentially set him up to fail which  is good news for him if it means that  denji stops being his roommate however  on the other hand I did mention in my  last video that Devils loses significant  amount of strength when they become  fiends so in theory power might not be  as strong as she thinks she is it's  equally possible that the reason they  haven't found any Devils is because  they're both just inexperienced and  maybe instead of setting denji up Aki  paired him with power so that he  wouldn't be the one looking after him  with that said episode 2 comes to an end  with power suddenly detecting the scent  of blood nearby and she quickly rushes  off leaving denji behind as he tries to  keep up she does some pretty impressive  parkour over the rooftops before  casually jumping off a building and in  this moment she activates her true power  one of her many abilities as the blood  devil is that she can manipulate her own  blood to create weapons and in this case  she transforms the blood coming out of  her wrist into a giant Mallet this  Mallet was made to crush the sea  cucumber devil down below but as we can  see there was already a civilian devil  Hunter dealing with the situation one of  the rules in Japan is that if a civilian  devil Hunter is involved with the devil  then it's illegal for Public Safety  double Hunters to just interfere and  kill it the reason for this rule is to  presumably protect the earnings of  Civilian Hunters who get paid based on  the Devils they capture and kill but in  this scene power just completely ignores  it as she splashes the sea cucumber in a  moment that was both colorful and  brilliantly animated now before we dive  into my personal rating for the episode  one thing I didn't find time to mention  was the painting in makima's office  which was visible as Aki pulled denji  across the floor this artwork seems to  be a similar style to the painting we  see in chapter 81 called the fall of  Lucifer which depicted Satan falling  from Heaven although the two paintings  aren't the same they definitely have the  same biblical tone so if you have any  idea where this new painting is from  then let me know in the comments Down  Below in terms of my thoughts on the  episode it did a lot of things that I  liked including amazing shots like the  one of makima's eye power destroying the  sea cucumber and the camera work on  Powers chess so I say that visually it  is more pleasing than episode 1. the one  thing I didn't like was that they  removed the muscle devil and don't get  me wrong I'm not pretending that this  was a big deal but I was kind of  surprised that they took it out  completely my guess is that they must  have like a specific point where they  won the the season to end and to reach  that point in the amount of episodes  they have I guess this was just a  necessary thing that had to be caught  however the reason I was surprised they  took it out is because last week during  episode one I mean that was the perfect  adaptation of the first chapter and so  to see such a huge chunk of episode two  you know being missing that was a big  shock overall though I'd still give this  episode a 9.5 out of 10. and if you want  these chainsaw man breakdowns to  continue then don't forget to hit that  sub button and drop a like if you're  feeling generous until the next one  peace out
 

